   $q$If the writer replaced sentence 14, which choice would best keep its role as the passage's conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sailors in earlier centuries had no way of measuring the sea quickly, so they relied on ropes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-only-introduction"},{"text":"The deepest trenches are so far down that sunlight never reaches the water at the bottom of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Long after sailors first dropped weighted ropes into the waves, the work of revealing the ocean floor is far from finished.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ocean currents, which carry warm and cold water around the globe, are another subject of research.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Long after sailors first dropped weighted ropes into the waves, the work of revealing the ocean floor is far from finished.$q$, $q$The correct choice echoes the opening image of the weighted rope and restates the point of sentence 13, that mapping is unfinished, which ties the whole passage together. The sentence about sailors in earlier centuries repeats only the first paragraph and ignores the unfinished work.$q$, 'draft', '169c0539-07a7-5d55-94db-fa3291c96318')
