   $q$A research summary reads: "The study of migratory songbirds revealed that many species, like, arrive earlier each spring." Which revision keeps a consistent formal style?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The study of migratory songbirds revealed that tons of species arrive earlier each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"The study of migratory songbirds revealed that many species arrive earlier each spring.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The study of migratory songbirds revealed that many species, you know, arrive earlier each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-filler"},{"text":"The study of migratory songbirds revealed that many species arrive later each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The study of migratory songbirds revealed that many species arrive earlier each spring.$q$, $q$Removing the filler "like" leaves a formal, accurate sentence. "Tons of species" removes the filler but adds a different casual phrase.$q$, 'draft', null)
