   $q$Read the sentence: "In the event that it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Should it be the case that it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase-remains"},{"text":"If it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Unless it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-relationship"},{"text":"In the case that it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase-remains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$If it rains, the outdoor orchestra concert will move to the gymnasium.$q$, $q$"If" replaces "In the event that" with no loss of meaning. "Unless" is also short, but it reverses the condition so the concert would move only when it does not rain.$q$, 'draft', null)
