   $q$Read the sentence: "A new exhibit on early mapmaking was designed by the students in the history club." The writer wants to emphasize the students as the people who did the work. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A new exhibit on early mapmaking was put together by the students in the history club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"passive-remains"},{"text":"Students in the history club visited a new exhibit on early mapmaking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"An exhibit on early mapmaking, which was new, was designed by students in the history club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"passive-remains"},{"text":"Students in the history club designed a new exhibit on early mapmaking.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Students in the history club designed a new exhibit on early mapmaking.$q$, $q$The active voice puts the students first as the doers and cuts "was designed by." The "visited" choice is active, but it says the students saw the exhibit rather than created it.$q$, 'draft', null)
