   $q$The researchers waited 48 hours before measuring the lake's oxygen levels. A draft says: "The researchers waited a while before measuring the lake's oxygen levels." Which revision is the most precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The researchers waited several days before measuring the lake's oxygen levels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"The researchers waited 48 hours before measuring the lake's oxygen levels.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The researchers waited a good amount of time before measuring the lake's oxygen levels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"The researchers waited 48 minutes before measuring the lake's oxygen levels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The researchers waited 48 hours before measuring the lake's oxygen levels.$q$, $q$"48 hours" gives the exact interval the stem reports. "Several days" sounds more specific than "a while," but it is still vague and does not match two days exactly.$q$, 'draft', null)
