   $q$The conductor rearranged the second movement because the orchestra's oboist fell ill. Which sentence expresses this relationship most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The orchestra's oboist fell ill, and the conductor also rearranged the second movement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loses-relationship"},{"text":"Because the orchestra's oboist fell ill, the conductor rearranged the second movement.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Although the orchestra's oboist fell ill, the conductor rearranged the second movement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-relationship"},{"text":"The orchestra's oboist fell ill, the conductor rearranged the second movement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the orchestra's oboist fell ill, the conductor rearranged the second movement.$q$, $q$"Because" makes the illness the clear cause of the change. "Although" sets up a contrast, which misstates how the two events are connected.$q$, 'draft', null)
