   $q$A reviewer wants to say that a historian's argument is convincing because each step follows logically from the evidence. Which word best completes the sentence "The historian's argument was ______: each claim followed logically from the documents she cited."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"eloquent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-nuance"},{"text":"contentious","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"},{"text":"cogent","is_correct":true},{"text":"verbose","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$cogent$q$, $q$"Cogent" means clear, logical, and convincing, which matches the explanation after the colon. "Eloquent" praises the beauty of the language, not the logic of the reasoning.$q$, 'draft', null)
