   $q$Read the sentences: "Mycorrhizae are networks of fungi. These networks link the roots of trees. They allow trees to exchange nutrients." Which revision uses an appositive to combine the ideas most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mycorrhizae are networks of fungi, they link the roots of trees and allow trees to exchange nutrients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"Networks of fungi that link tree roots allow mycorrhizae to exchange nutrients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"Mycorrhizae, networks of fungi, allow trees to exchange nutrients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"},{"text":"Mycorrhizae, networks of fungi that link tree roots, allow trees to exchange nutrients.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mycorrhizae, networks of fungi that link tree roots, allow trees to exchange nutrients.$q$, $q$The appositive "networks of fungi that link tree roots" defines the term inside the sentence and keeps all three facts. The choice "Mycorrhizae, networks of fungi, allow trees to exchange nutrients" also uses an appositive but loses the detail that the networks link roots.$q$, 'draft', null)
