   $q$Organizers changed the marathon route so that runners would go around a construction zone instead of through it. Which word most precisely completes the sentence "The new route was designed to ______ the construction zone."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"surpass","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-word"},{"text":"bypass","is_correct":true},{"text":"traverse","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"circumscribe","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$bypass$q$, $q$"Bypass" means to go around something, which is what the new route does. "Traverse" means to cross through, the opposite of the organizers' goal, and "circumscribe" means to draw a boundary around something.$q$, 'draft', null)
