   $q$Read the sentences: "Lichen grows extremely slowly. Some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old. Scientists can use them to date the walls." Which choice most effectively combines the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lichen grows extremely slowly, some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old, scientists can use them to date the walls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Lichen grows extremely slowly, some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old; a fact that lets scientists use them to date the walls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"Although lichen grows extremely slowly, some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old, a fact that lets scientists date the walls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"illogical-connector"},{"text":"Lichen grows so slowly that some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old, a fact that lets scientists use them to date the walls.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lichen grows so slowly that some patches on the old stone walls may be centuries old, a fact that lets scientists use them to date the walls.$q$, $q$"So slowly that" shows cause and effect in one correct sentence, and the phrase "a fact that lets scientists" attaches with a comma. "Although" signals contrast, but slow growth is the reason the patches are old, not a contrast with it.$q$, 'draft', null)
