  ('fd2052ef-ac29-546e-81e9-a47259000a72', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence, placed in the blank at sentence 8, would best support Baek's claim in sentence 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Baek found that many farm families in the county could not afford to buy books of their own at the time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-rejected-explanation"},{"text":"Baek found that more than half of the books lent after 1910 were titles listed in Fairweather's request notebook.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Baek found that the county built a brick library in town in 1921, the same year the wagon stopped running.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-claim"},{"text":"Baek found that the wagon traveled about thirty miles a week on dirt roads that turned to mud each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Baek found that more than half of the books lent after 1910 were titles listed in Fairweather's request notebook.$q$, $q$The claim is that the wagon succeeded because it responded to requests, and the notebook finding ties the rising loans directly to those requests. The point about families being unable to afford books supports the "closer to readers" explanation that Baek says is not enough.$q$, 'draft', 'd95e0f64-caa6-5efb-83c0-0c458f6a3d65')
